{{Card Infobox|Cost=3|Rarity=Rare|Type=Building|Arena=Bone Pit|ReleaseDate=4 January 2016}}
{{Quote|Building that periodically spawns Skeletons to fight the enemy... and when destroyed, spawns 4 more Skeletons! Creepy.}}

The Tombstone is a {{Rarity|Rare}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Bone Pit (Arena 2)]]. It spawns a [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] with moderate hitpoints. Every 3.5 seconds, the Tombstone will passively summon a group of two [[Skeletons]], with a 0.5 seconds delay from each other. When destroyed, it will also spawn four Skeletons. A Tombstone card costs 3 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Tombstone Card}}
*The spawned [[Skeletons]] are very effective at distracting single-targeting, slow hit speed enemy [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] such as the [[P.E.K.K.A.]], the [[Prince]], the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], and the [[Giant Skeleton]]. This is especially effective against units that target [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]], such as the [[Giant]] and [[Golem]]; the Skeletons spawned after the Tombstone's destruction can heavily damage, if not completely destroy the unit.
**In the case of the Golem, the Golem's death damage may defeat the Skeletons and the Golemites may deal some damage to the [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|Crown Tower]].
**It can also distract other units for a while, such as the [[Princess]] or [[Mortar]].
**If any other ranged troop is locked onto a Tower, the player can use the Tombstone to push the troop so it retargets on to the Tombstone. This cannot be done with any defensive building as they do not have a large enough hitbox to push the troops, but the Tombstone works because the spawned Skeletons have enough hitbox space to push the troops. The Skeletons will then chip away at the troop's health.
*As a general rule of thumb, all buildings except for the [[Elixir Collector]] should be placed near the center of the player's territory so that enemy troops are drawn further away from the player's Crown Towers, while keeping them close enough so that both Crown Towers can assist in chipping down the troops. A placement 4 tiles from the river staggered into the lane of the player's weaker Crown Tower is sufficient against building targeting troops.
*Unlike other spawner buildings, the Tombstone should not be placed behind the Crown Towers. Its spawned Skeletons are not potent enough to justify protecting the building with the Crown Towers, and any spells that the opponent uses on it can also mildly chip the Crown Tower's health. Instead, it is more effective to be used to protect the Crown Towers from dangerous incoming troops. Despite this, it can still be effective at distracting a [[Miner]] placed next to the Crown Towers.
*The Tombstone can spawn up to 20 Skeletons, 16 of which are spawned normally over the lifetime of the Tombstone. It then spawns 4 more when it is destroyed. A [[Skeleton Army]] costs the same amount of Elixir and spawns 5 less Skeletons, but the Tombstone is not as vulnerable to splash units or spells as the Tombstone's Skeletons spawn periodically as opposed to all at once, but cannot deal any damage to a Tower alone unlike the Skeleton Army.
*If the opponent plays their [[Hog Rider]] at the edge of the [[Arenas|Arena]] to bypass the player's Tombstone, they can place the Tombstone 1 tile higher to catch it every time. However, this makes the Tombstone much more vulnerable to being sniped by ranged units across the river.
*The Tombstone is useful for soaking up the [[Wall Breakers]]' powerful damage, although causing a slight negative [[Elixir]] trade.
*The Tombstone is rather ineffective against [[Bowler|Bowlers]] and [[Executioner|Executioners]], since their projectiles have the ability to pierce which not only destroy the building but also to destroy the recently spawned Skeletons.
*The Tombstone should not be placed when the troop you want to distract has area damage troops or spells supporting it, as the Tombstone will quickly be eliminated.
*One should not place this card in a lane offensively without any support since the Skeletons it spawns get destroyed by Crown Towers in 1 shot and do not function well as cover troops.
*[[The Log]] can be an excellent counter to a Tombstone placed in the center of the Arena. If it is deployed when the Tombstone's hitpoints are below 50%, it can not only destroy the Tombstone but also destroy the Skeletons that spawn upon its destruction.
**The [[Barbarian Barrel]] can destroy the Tombstone similarly to The Log, and spawns a [[Barbarians|Barbarian]] to attack the Crown Towers. However, it cannot reach the Tombstone if it is placed too deep within the enemy's territory.
**If the player does not have The Log, [[Arrows]] can be used to counter it for a neutral Elixir trade. However, the player must decide whether to prioritize the spawner itself or its death spawn; unlike The Log, Arrows cannot hit both.
**[[Earthquake]] is a more powerful counter than Arrows, destroying a Tombstone in 2 hits, and defeating the spawned Skeletons on the third for the same Elixir cost.
**[[Fireball]] can also destroy the Tombstone no matter its current health. However, it is usually a negative Elixir trade unless the player is able to hit something else too, and it cannot hit the spawned Skeletons. [[Poison]] will also destroy the Tombstone over its full duration and also take care of the death spawn.
**Other spells like the [[Zap]] and [[Giant Snowball]], while ineffective against the Tombstone itself, are still useful for clearing the Skeletons that spawn after death. This is useful when you want to clear the path for an attacking unit that the Tombstone is used to distract, such as a Prince.
*In the [[Global Spell|Rage Challenge]], all buildings' (including the Tombstone's) lifetimes are unaffected, but in Tombstone's case, the Troop producing speed is, allowing it to produce up to 10.5 waves of Skeletons instead of the usual 8 in the challenge.

